    SIGNED deflection from 0.5:  rate -0.0926   burst +0.1228
    naming needs 0.153 (230 Hz of separation on a 750 Hz lerp)

    THE SIGNS ARE OPPOSED, which is the finding. rate - burst would
    ADD the deflections: 0.2154, or 1.41x the 0.153 naming needs.
    DO NOT BUILD ON THAT YET: these are BETWEEN-creature SEs, and burst
    events run 0.44 Hz against ~4.5 Hz of spikes. A sparse centroid's
    PER-FRAME noise is the same trade that refused the two-pool readout
    and it must be measured on the covariance before anything is built.

    REFUSED ON MAGNITUDE -- the burst profile IS less flat (0.1228 vs
    0.0926) but reaches only 80% of the 0.153 naming needs. A readout
    change costs recalibration of every vocal number; this does not pay
    for it ALONE. Read it with the opposed-signs note above.

